how do you deal with jealous co-workers  if you have a full-time job if you're  working somewhere and you have a dream  to start your own thing you're going to  find that the people you're working with  often will be jealous of what you're  doing because they want to do the same  thing but they don't have the guts to go  out and do it some people will be  supportive and others will just be  flat-out jealous you can't let their  jealousy their hatred their negativity  towards you hold you back from making  something great their opinions are  irrelevant I've got a great question  from one of our readers Cornell who  wrote in with that problems there's a  full-time job starting a filmmaking  business and all of the coworkers are  really jealous of what's going on  and the question is how do I handle this  how do I handle the ignorance and the  awkward jokes and the jealousy that come  from my co-workers so I want to share  with you a couple of coping mechanisms  that can help and and what helped me  when I was starting my business one  nugget of wisdom that will share with me  a long time ago by by a friend when  dealing with people who you're having an  argument with is try to imagine like  they're a baby or really really old  person because we tend to have more  patience right if there's if there's a  baby who's yelling at you or  three-year-olds was yelling at you who  doesn't understand the difference  necessarily between right or wrong you  have a little bit more patience so  somebody's coming at you with a lot of  negativity try to just imagine them as  being an ignorant three-year-old  and have a little more patience so  that's first the second you can decide  not to share right I mean it's great  that you are starting your business  while you're still at your job right  it's a great way to start a business  make sure that you're going to earn an  income from it and then move off and  eventually become full-time on your own  but in the meantime if people are hating  around you then just don't share don't  share what's going on in your business  with them don't share all the big wins  that you're having because it's only  going to cause more negativity the third  option is if you're going to share don't  just share the good stuff show them the  pain  show them the vulnerability show them  that you're scared children that you  have no idea what you're doing  show them that you're in way over  head nobody wants to beat up on somebody  to win they're down right there jealous  of you and they're there throwing  punches at you because they think you're  off to a better place and they're  jealous right they want to go with you  they want to do that for themselves but  they're not able to do it they don't  have the guts to do it shatter the  illusion that this is a perfect world  that this is so easy and you're making  tons of money like this is really hard  and you're scared and if you share that  with them it's really hard to get on  somebody and make fun of them if they're  sharing that they're really scared about  something but if you come in and you're  acting all tough and and you just landed  this big deal and you're bragging about  it then of course people are going to  hate on you and they're going to be  really jealous  I'll make jokes but if you're being  really vulnerable and really real then  it breaks down the walls a little bit  and they won't be as quick to criticize  you okay the last option here is to just  ignore them you know what you're doing  your thing you're building your dream  you're doing the right thing you're  passionate what you're doing you're  helping people you know you're not going  to be there for very long at that job  you're going to have your own company  doing great things ignore the haters  because you're going to have them always  in your business if it's not the  full-time people who are you're working  with it's going to be other people  around you there's always going to be  people who are jealous of what you're  doing it has nothing to do with you with  their own insecurities and you can lap  them off and ignore them because you  know you're doing the right thing one  thing that really helped me when I was  getting my business started I was in  University and I had a really tough  decision as to whether I should start my  own business I was running there already  part-time I didn't know if I should jump  into that full-time or if I should go  get a job and I had interviewed with  some really successful companies and  thought maybe I should go work for them  I wasn't entirely sure what to do with  my career and all of my friends were  going that route they were all getting  jobs and so that's really it's really  hard to go the other way you know when  your friends are all doing one thing and  you're the only black sheep it's really  hard to have the courage in Fortitude to  go a different direction and so what I  did was  some friends were really encouraging and  some friends were jealous and thought it  was stupid for doing my own thing  instead of taking a high paying job it's  really important that you create an  environment for yourself  that builds you up that lifts you up and  that's from the friends that you hang  out with that's when the family members  who are around you that's from the books  you read the websites you visit the  things that you listen to and the people  and the information that do not support  you you illuminate for your life you  know if you have friends that just keep  hating on you and saying what a bad idea  this is maybe they shouldn't be your  friends anymore right what kind of  friend does that now you may not have a  whole lot of options right now these are  your co-workers and hopefully eventually  are going to move and become your own  boss and not have to deal with people  who you don't want to deal with but at  the same time build up a network around  you of people who do believe in what  you're doing talk to 